{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1554470-nuradi-biospheres","id":1554470,"title":"Nuradi Biospheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-19T01:16:52-07:00","id":1554470,"title":"Nuradi Biospheres","content":"So, Ive got some more vague ideas about how to stretch and flex some of the setting of Autocthonia to incorporate more sci-fi settings. This one is an idea I had, based on some of 2e's lore, that I think could still be a lot of fun to tinker with. I thought I'd spitball and brainstorm a bit on here, based on potential &quot;storyteller prerogative&quot; to push some things in interesting ways. So..<br /> <br /> Nurad was once a nation on the cutting edge. Perfect Hydraulic Grace was a mystery--hollistic, naturalistic, transhumanistic, practical, simple. In the Progressive Era, Nurad was at the forefront of many technologies that resembled the heights of First Age magic and technology. Legend says that, before the Silent Era and Shuttered Lamp Wars, that Nurad had succesfully cloned and re-established biological beings from Creation. Pigs, pigeons, rice, trees.. whole Metropoli were dedicated to the Genesis Arts. In the early days, the Nuradi came to grips with invasive species-- Nurad is one of the few parts of Autocthonia with pigeons, for example, though evem they have spread and established themselves in other nations by now. The sheer size of the Nuradisphere has allowed soils and dust and water to accumulate in its nooks and cranies, and life takes root here more often than the rest of Autocthonia. Even if much of Nurad more closely resembles a desert, filled with canyons and mesas caked with dust and stone-caking, some parts of it have self sustained ecosystems.<br /> <br /> While the Silent Era and Shuttered Lamp Wars saw Ludites trying to eradicate such invasive species, that is far from nation wide. Some Metropoli felt that the remnants of Creation were LESS blasphemous than other technologies, and thus even today closely resemble modern Creation's small farming communities, surviving on farming and animal husbandry. Gateway Folk are especially famous for understanding the living parts of their ecosystem, and trade such secrets for technology in cities. During the growing resource crisis, both Progressives and Conservatives look to those lost Genesis arts with interest.<br /> <br /> But not all Metropoli experimenting with Genesis Arts were within the Nuradisphere directly. Some were seen as bold and dangerous, even in the days before Perygra's Fall. Perygra worked with a few of her pupils to establish Genesis-based experimental Metropoli on both the Leading and Trailing edge of the Sphere. Some were considerably more advanced than simply cloning pig-knuckles and rice. Lost records hint that there are entire colonies, just past the range of invasive species, attached to Nurad. Each was based on recreating environments within Creation. Most required a Wood Demense, already hard to come by within Autocthonia. Each Alchemical who lead the project of a Biodome tailored their Charms to support it. Each was a miracle of Genesis arts and advanced worship. Some used direct Conduits from the Materium Tabernacle or the pole of Steam to power whatever biology required. Some, it is said, even tapped into the Void, and used the chaos to mutate Machine into Life.<br /> <br /> Today? Do with it what you will. A long lost Garden on the leading edge, a utopia using gremlins and chaos to actually make a living ecosystem? A simple farming community being taking advantage of by its nearby conduit-dry Metropolis? An excuse for a jungle-but-cyberpunk city? An entire miniaturized bacteria-sized Metropolis designed long ago to prevent disease, Innerspace style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"